Expanded story:
On a sunny morning in Willow Creek, Amy stirred eggs into a sizzling pan while Will and Amber chased each other around the kitchen table. The clatter of spoons was suddenly interrupted by a groaning sound at the front door; a zombie had broken through the cracked window. Without hesitation, Amy grabbed Will’s hand and pushed Amber toward the back bedroom—her makeshift safe room with its heavy door locked tight—and ushered them inside as the undead creature lunged for her.

She slipped out of the kitchen in one breath, stepping onto the worn floorboards that led to the living room where she could hear the zombie’s thudding footsteps. In a quick dash back across the hallway, Amy returned to the kitchen and pulled open the pantry door, revealing her hidden arsenal: a pistol tucked behind a stack of canned beans and a gleaming katana slid out from beneath the fridge.

The house erupted in chaos as more zombies burst through the front windows and doors, their eyes fixed on her. With pistol in one hand and katana in the other, Amy fought each intruder one by one—shooting at the nearest with precise shots, then slashing the others to splintered flesh. New zombies kept arriving from every corner, but she met them all head‑on, never letting a single creature breach her defenses.

When the last zombie fell, its body collapsing onto the hardwood floor in a splash of blood and sweat, Amy wiped her hands on the back of her shirt and stepped out toward the back bedroom. She opened the door to find Will and Amber waiting for her, eyes wide but safe behind the locked latch. Together they slipped past the remaining zombies that had gathered at the hallway’s end, stepping into the cool night air beyond the house with their mother leading them home again.
